The best pieces bind on pickup, so you must craft them yourself. Mail recipes are not usable by a Rogue."},{n="Skinning",b="Leather and hides for Leatherworking, or easy early income for training costs.",cv="Gathering only; no direct combat bonus."},{n="Engineering",b="Grenades, explosives and devices that add to an already strong control kit; Recommended for PvP. Gnomes fail fewer engineering devices.",cv="Pairs with Mining. Guns and scopes only improve Shoot, which a Rogue uses for pulling."},{n="Alchemy",b="Agility and Strength elixirs, healing potions and protection potions for hard fights.",cv="Ordinary healing potions are also First Aid crafts in Forever; discolored Alchemy potions have a different effect."},{n="Herbalism",b="Herbs for Alchemy or income. Sap and Vanish let a Rogue gather herbs past enemies, even inside dungeons.",cv="Swiftthistle for Thistle Tea is a bonus herb from Mageroyal and Briarthorn."},{n="Mining",b="Ore and stone for Blacksmithing or Engineering, and income from bars.",cv="No direct combat bonus beyond the gathering itself."},{n=S[60],b="Rough Sharpening Stones and Rough Weightstones early, which have a big impact at low level, plus daggers, swords, axes and maces to compare.",cv="You can buy the stones instead. Most plate and mail recipes are of no use to a Rogue."},{n="Cooking",b="Buff food that adds stats and extra experience from kills; Thistle Tea (Cooking 60, from the poison quest) restores 100 Energy.",cv="Thistle Tea has a 5-minute cooldown."},{n="First Aid",b="Bandages, healing potions and Anti-Venom. Rogues have no healing spells, so this is the main way to recover in a fight: Blind or Gouge, then bandage.",cv="Damage interrupts bandaging."},{n="Fishing",b="Fish for Cooking, including buff-food ingredients.",cv="No guaranteed income is implied."}},gearBrackets={{b="Quest rewards",no="Dungeon quests whose Rogue-usable rewards are recorded in the Forever database. Quest rewards carry no level requirement of their own, so each 